swing-mcp-agent.jar — NOT IN THIS RELEASE
=========================================

What would be here
------------------
The SwingBridge MCP agent: a `-javaagent` you attach to your *unmigrated* Swing app,
which exposes the running app's accessibility tree and its interactions over MCP. An
agent can then drive the desktop app and write down what it does — the "before" side of
behavioural verification, which you check the migrated browser app against afterwards.

Why it is not here yet
----------------------
It has no release train of its own yet, so there is no versioned jar for this kit to
carry. Bundling a build off a maintainer's machine would give you a binary nobody can
reproduce, which is worse than an honest gap.

What to do meanwhile
--------------------
Build it from source:

    git clone https://github.com/vaadin/swing-mcp
    cd swing-mcp && ./mvnw -C clean package

Then attach the jar it produces to your Swing app's JVM. The example apps' READMEs under
testapps/ show where the flag goes for each of them — note that it belongs on the *app's*
JVM, not on Maven's, which is why they build a jar and launch it directly rather than
using `exec:java`.

Nothing else in this kit depends on this file. When it lands, it lands at exactly this
path, minus the `.placeholder` suffix.
